## UI/UX QUALITY STANDARD — INVESTOR DEMO GRADE

This app must be built to **investor demo grade AND production ready** at all times.
Every screen, every widget, every interaction must meet this standard — there is no
"placeholder for now" or "we'll polish this later." Every screen is potentially the
first screen an investor sees.

### What this means concretely:

**Completeness — no detail may be skipped:**
- Every label, badge, status indicator, icon, and piece of copy specified in the
  designs must be implemented exactly as described.
- Every state must be handled: loading, empty, error, success, partial data.
- If a design specifies a shimmer loader — build a shimmer loader.
- If a design specifies an inline action button — build the inline action button.
- If a design specifies a deadline countdown — build the deadline countdown.
- Skipping, stubbing, or using a TODO placeholder for any UI detail is NOT acceptable.

**Improvement is allowed — omission is not:**
- Cursor may improve animations, transitions, micro-interactions, and visual polish
  beyond what the designs specify — but ONLY in addition to the specified details,
  never instead of them.
- If Cursor identifies a better UX pattern for a specific interaction, it may
  implement it AND note the improvement — but the original specified behaviour
  must still be present unless explicitly replacing it makes the UX unambiguously better.

**Production readiness:**
- Every screen handles all edge cases (null data, empty lists, network errors,
  expired sessions, permission denials).
- No debug prints, no hardcoded test data, no Lorem Ipsum text in any screen.
- All tap targets meet minimum 48x48dp touch target size.
- All text meets WCAG AA contrast ratio against its background.
- All images use CachedNetworkImage with shimmer placeholders and error fallbacks.
- All lists use proper pagination or infinite scroll — never load unbounded data.
- All forms validate inputs before submission.
- All async operations show loading state and handle errors gracefully.

