## TESTING RULES

- Unit tests for all use cases (domain layer)
- Unit tests for all repository implementations (with mock data sources)
- Widget tests for critical screens (payment checkout, bid outcome)
- Integration tests for auth flow
- Use `mocktail` for mocking
- Test files in `test/` mirroring `lib/` structure

---

## DO NOT

- Do NOT call Firestore directly from presentation layer (screens/notifiers)
- Do NOT import Firebase packages in domain layer
- Do NOT hardcode Firestore collection names — use `FirestoreCollections` constants
- Do NOT hardcode exchange rates or cost defaults
- Do NOT use get_it or injectable — Riverpod only for DI
- Do NOT use the Provider package — Riverpod only
- Do NOT create global chat or document screens — these are per-order
- Do NOT allow buyers to create payment requests
- Do NOT allow edit/cancel when `firstPaymentMade = true`
- Do NOT use `setState` in screens that have Riverpod providers
- Do NOT put business logic in widgets
- Do NOT use dark backgrounds — all backgrounds are white or off-white
- Do NOT implement dark mode
- Do NOT skip any UI detail specified in the designs — implement everything
- Do NOT use Lorem Ipsum, placeholder text, or hardcoded test data in any screen
- Do NOT use `print()` or debug prints in production code — use proper logging
- Do NOT leave TODO comments in UI code — implement it or raise it explicitly
- Do NOT use system fonts — always use DM Sans via `google_fonts`
